BT /F1 12 Tf 56 782 Td (HTML, XHTML, and XML: A Comparison) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 56 764 Td (Rewritten response) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 56 746 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 56 728 Td (HTML provides the elements used to structure content for browsers.) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 56 710 Td (Its parsing rules are designed to make webpages widely accessible.) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 56 692 Td (XHTML keeps HTML vocabulary but follows stricter XML well-formedness.) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 56 674 Td (For example, elements must close and nesting must be correct.) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 56 656 Td (XML is a general data format that lets authors define meaningful tags.) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 56 638 Td (It carries information between systems rather than styling a page.) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 56 620 Td (Thus, HTML focuses on rendering, XHTML on strict web documents,) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 56 602 Td (and XML on representing and exchanging structured data.) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 56 584 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 56 566 Td (The best choice depends on whether the goal is display or data.) Tj ET
